✧ «The Table of Paradise» or «The Heavenly Feast» – pen-and-ink drawing on the “back” of the glass
(At the client's request, the two saints invited to «The Heavenly Feast» are Saint Anne and Saint Constantine)

• The iconographic theme divides the space of the composition into five rhombus-shaped fields separated by decorated bands;
• The Mother of God with the Child and Jesus Christ blessing are always in the upper rhombuses and cannot be replaced;
• Saint Paraskeva and Saint Nicholas are usually in the lower rhombuses and can be replaced
• So, for a personalised icon, you choose two saints (or just one) for the two lower rhombuses (or for just one of them)
